{"id": "L01-W1", "lane": "L01", "title": "The formation law is not fixed: one rule, many laws", "plain": "The axiom says a site's odds depend on its neighbours. But neighbours form at different times, so which ones count as already there depends on the order sites form, whether neighbours form together, and how unrecorded sites are treated. Each choice gives a different law from the same rule, and the all-at-once (static) law is none of them once a loop exists. The axioms do not pick the order.", "severity": "blocking", "status": "open", "evidence": ["/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/admissibility-induced-law-decision-record.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/formation-3plus1-lead.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/formation-reading-is-the-axiom.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/induced-law-blocks-01-52-index.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/probe-harvest-20260919.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_FORMATION_ORDER_MENU_ORDER_MIXTURE_MONOTONE_BOX_AND_CUBE_CENSUS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-13.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_COVARIANCE_FORCES_A_REVERSIBLE_FORMATION_LAW_THREE_COVARIANT_PASTS_AND_THE_SIX_NEIGHBOUR_PAST_SETTLES_INTO_TWO_COPIES_OF_THE_STATIC_LAW_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-23.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_FINITE_UNRECORDED_COMPONENT_FACTORIZATION_AND_ATTACHMENT_FACTORS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-15.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_FORMATION_LAW_VERSUS_STATIC_LAW_FINITE_WINDOW_CLASSIFICATION_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-06.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_FORMATION_RATE_IDENTITIES_AND_FINITE_WINDOW_WITNESSES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-15.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_FORMATION_UNIT_CONDITIONAL_IDENTITIES_AND_FINITE_WITNESSES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-15.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_HOW_RECORDS_FORM_STATIC_LAW_OUTSIDE_THE_HULL_OF_ADAPTED_FORMATION_LAWS_AND_CLAUSE_INDEPENDENCE_ON_A_CAUSAL_PREDECESSOR_STRUCTURE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-20.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_RE_RECORDING_AT_EVERY_TICK_STATIC_LAW_STATIONARY_LIGHT_CONE_BILAYER_LONG_RANGE_ORDER_GREEN_FUNCTION_RESPONSE_CONDITIONAL_ON_AN_EXCLUDED_CLAUSE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-20.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THREE_READINGS_OF_RECORDS_FORM_AGAINST_KNOWN_PHYSICS_THE_SPACETIME_READING_IS_TWO_DIMENSIONAL_SKEWED_AND_IRREVERSIBLE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-23.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/NN_FORMATION_SELECTOR_TWO_MODEL_KILL_BOUNDED_NOTE_2026-08-14.md", "docs/RECORD_FORMATION_NOT_UNCONDITIONALLY_FORCED_BY_MINIMAL_AXIOMS_NARROW_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-06.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L02", "L04", "L14", "L01-W2"]}
{"id": "L01-W2", "lane": "L01", "title": "No rule for where, when and how fast records form", "plain": "The axioms say records form, not at which site, at what rate, or in what numbers. Written as a mathematical birth process, the allowed rules form a whole family (six free rates for a cube-symmetric one), and nothing picks one. What a sealed box freezes into, and whether that is one state or exponentially many, is decided by the rule you supply, not by the axioms.", "severity": "blocking", "status": "open", "evidence": ["docs/ACTION_TRANSFER_RECORD_HAZARD_CONTENT_CROSSCALIBRATION_BOUNDARY_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-02.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_BINDING_SCALE_PINNED_AT_THE_NEUTRAL_VALUE_PAIR_WEIGHT_IS_THE_RULES_LIKELIHOOD_RATIO_NO_BINDING_WITHOUT_A_CYCLE_ALL_BINDING_IS_AGREEMENT_AROUND_LOOPS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-20.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_RECORDS_THAT_MOVE_PAIR_WEIGHT_TRANSIT_HAS_THE_STATIC_LAW_AS_EQUILIBRIUM_THE_BINDING_SCALE_IS_A_NEW_CONSTANT_CLUMPING_AND_JAMMING_EXECUTED_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-20.md", "docs/A_FORMATION_RATE_RULER_EVADES_THE_SEAS_SUBLATTICE_CANCELLATION_AND_THE_BRIDGES_CONSTANT_MODE_FIXES_KAPPA_R_EQUALS_ONE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-04.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORD_FORMATION_NOT_UNCONDITIONALLY_FORCED_BY_MINIMAL_AXIOMS_NARROW_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-06.md", "docs/RECORD_NATIVE_MARKED_PURE_BIRTH_RESOURCE_GENERATOR_BOUNDARY_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-08-14.md", "docs/RECORD_PERMANENCE_FORCES_FRESH_SITE_DOUBLE_REGISTRATION_AND_AGREEMENT_SURVIVAL_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-07-11.md", "docs/RECORD_PRODUCTION_KERNEL_BOUNDARY_2026-06-06.md", "docs/THE_OWNERS_FROZEN_BOX_READING_WITH_COUNT_THRESHOLD_FORMATION_RULES_UPWARD_RULES_FREEZE_INTO_ONE_STATE_CROWDING_RULES_INTO_MANY_EXACT_SMALL_BOX_COUNTS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-29.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L04", "L14", "L15", "L13", "L01-W1", "L01-W3"]}
{"id": "L01-W3", "lane": "L01", "title": "Records cannot be born by a unitary wave with Born count statistics", "plain": "Suppose the quantum wave evolves reversibly and the number of records follows the wave's odds. Then a count that never falls never rises, because a reversible rule that creates also destroys. Records could move but not appear. The owner's picture, where the count rises until the box freezes, therefore needs something outside this: a non-reversible step, count odds that are not the wave's, or records that can also die.", "severity": "major", "status": "open", "evidence": ["/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/records-count-rises-until-frozen.md", "docs/ARROW_FROM_RECORD_FORMATION_PAST_HYPOTHESIS_RESIDUAL_NOTE_2026-06-05.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md", "docs/UNDER_A_UNITARY_WAVE_WITH_BORN_COUNT_STATISTICS_A_RECORD_COUNT_THAT_NEVER_FALLS_NEVER_RISES_RECORDS_CANNOT_FORM_FROM_NOTHING_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-28.md"], "same_as": ["L03", "L15", "L04", "L02", "L01-W2", "L01-W4", "L01-W7"]}
{"id": "L01-W4", "lane": "L01", "title": "A sharp one-site birth costs the energy of its bonds, which heat budgets rule out", "plain": "If a record is a sharp lock of one site, it cuts that site's bonds. The energy is about 2 to 3.7 bond energies for Heisenberg qubits, or 2.4 hop energies for the walker sea. With the lattice tied to the speed of light, that is gigajoules per record at the Planck scale, and at 1e-19 m Earth's heat allows only about 2e-5 births per kg per second. Sharp births look unphysical at every spacing.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced (equivalent to a named premise)", "evidence": ["docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORD_FORMATION_A_SHARP_ONE_SITE_LOCK_COSTS_THE_ENERGY_OF_ITS_BONDS_IN_THE_WALKERS_SEA_ABOUT_TWO_POINT_FOUR_LATTICE_ENERGY_UNITS_PER_RECORD_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L03", "L16", "L13", "L15", "L01-W3", "L01-W5"]}
{"id": "L01-W5", "lane": "L01", "title": "Redundant readability of a record (local observability) is not derived", "plain": "The axioms make records permanent and readable only through records. They do not make a record readable by many independent observers, the 'copies everywhere' property that makes a fact objective. This has been an open gate since June. Tests on the lattice's own rules failed: a single site's bit scrambles into its surroundings instead of being copied.", "severity": "major", "status": "open", "evidence": ["docs/DARWINISM_BRIDGE_RESIDUAL_LOCAL_OBSERVABILITY_OPEN_GATE_NOTE_2026-06-05.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORD_BLANK_BOUNDARY_RESET_NO_GO_2026-06-05.md", "docs/RECORD_FORMATION_A_SHARP_ONE_SITE_LOCK_COSTS_THE_ENERGY_OF_ITS_BONDS_IN_THE_WALKERS_SEA_ABOUT_TWO_POINT_FOUR_LATTICE_ENERGY_UNITS_PER_RECORD_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md", "docs/REDUNDANCY_NOT_FORCED_BY_PND_LOCALITY_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-08.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md", "scripts/redundant_records_under_the_heisenberg_rule_on_a_uniform_patch_2026_09_27.py", "scripts/redundant_records_with_a_pointer_impurity_in_the_free_sea_2026_09_28.py"], "same_as": ["L03", "L01-W3", "L01-W6"]}
{"id": "L01-W6", "lane": "L01", "title": "The arrow of time needs a low-record past", "plain": "Records give the arrow its direction, away from the state with fewest records. But the framework does not supply that starting state, and its equations run equally well backwards. Start from a high-record state and the arrow reverses. 'Begin with few records' is an extra input, the same as physics' past hypothesis. Closed reversible rules cannot prepare a blank starting register either.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced (equivalent to a named premise)", "evidence": ["docs/ARROW_CPT_ORIENTATION_DO_NOT_SOURCE_CP_ODD_ACTION_COEFFICIENTS_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-08.md", "docs/ARROW_FROM_RECORD_FORMATION_PAST_HYPOTHESIS_RESIDUAL_NOTE_2026-06-05.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/PAST_HYPOTHESIS_EXISTENCE_REDUCTION_APPEND_ONLY_WELL_FOUNDEDNESS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-11.md", "docs/RECORD_BLANK_BOUNDARY_RESET_NO_GO_2026-06-05.md", "docs/RECORD_BLANK_SINK_PREPARATION_REGRESS_NO_GO_2026-06-05.md", "docs/TIME_AXIS_IS_THE_HISTORY_INDEX_RECORD_MONOTONE_DIRECTION_BOUNDED_NOTE_2026-07-03.md", "docs/UNDER_A_UNITARY_WAVE_WITH_BORN_COUNT_STATISTICS_A_RECORD_COUNT_THAT_NEVER_FALLS_NEVER_RISES_RECORDS_CANNOT_FORM_FROM_NOTHING_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-28.md", "docs/ai_methodology/skills/PRIMITIVE_REGISTRY_CHECK.md"], "same_as": ["L04", "L13", "L11", "L01-W3", "L01-W5"]}
{"id": "L01-W7", "lane": "L01", "title": "Records alone cannot give quantum correlations; a wave with nonlocal odds is a second ingredient", "plain": "If records form locally and causally from records alone, their correlations cannot exceed the classical bound (CHSH 2), while quantum mechanics reaches 2.83. A wave over the records reproduces the quantum correlations, but then the odds for a record's next move depend on distant records, and the state is no longer just a configuration of records.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced (equivalent to a named premise)", "evidence": ["docs/DYNAMICS_CLAUSE_BELL_VALUES_OF_RECORD_LAWS_RECORDS_ONLY_FORMATION_STAYS_AT_TWO_THE_DYNAMICS_CLAUSE_REACHES_TWO_ROOT_TWO_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md", "docs/DYNAMICS_CLAUSE_CAMPAIGN_SYNTHESIS_WHAT_ONE_LOCAL_DYNAMICS_CLAUSE_BUYS_AND_WHAT_IT_LEAVES_OPEN_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md", "docs/DYNAMICS_CLAUSE_RECORDS_ONLY_ADMISSIBILITY_LEAVES_THE_DYNAMICS_UNREADABLE_FORMING_SITES_MUST_BE_ISOLATED_AND_NEVER_INTERACT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORDS_AS_BEABLES_UNDER_THE_MOVING_RECORDS_READING_BELLS_JUMP_LAW_GIVES_NEAREST_NEIGHBOUR_MOVES_EQUIVARIANT_ODDS_AND_BELL_CORRELATIONS_WITH_NONLOCAL_ODDS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L03", "L02", "L01-W3", "L01-W10"]}
{"id": "L01-W8", "lane": "L01", "title": "The record layer alone is diffusive: waves, inertia and 1/r fields need another layer", "plain": "Records governed by non-negative odds, like the axiom's distribution, spread out and settle. They do not oscillate. A wave needs signed amplitudes, and inertia or a long-range force needs a rule that is second order in time. So a record can be a source, with mass equal to the record count, but the field it makes has to live in an amplitude layer the axioms do not name.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced (equivalent to a named premise)", "evidence": ["/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/admissibility-induced-law-block41.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/probe-harvest-20260919.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THREE_READINGS_OF_RECORDS_FORM_AGAINST_KNOWN_PHYSICS_THE_SPACETIME_READING_IS_TWO_DIMENSIONAL_SKEWED_AND_IRREVERSIBLE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-23.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_WAVES_AMONG_MOVING_RECORDS_NEED_A_COUPLING_THAT_TIME_REVERSAL_FLIPS_CLOCKED_RECORD_MOTION_NEVER_OSCILLATES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-23.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_WAVES_NEED_SIGNED_WEIGHTS_A_FORMATION_RULE_WITH_NONNEGATIVE_WEIGHTS_KEEPS_AN_UNDAMPED_BRANCH_ONLY_BY_RIGID_TRANSPORT_AND_THE_AMPLITUDE_STEP_IS_A_SIGNED_RULE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_WHAT_A_SOURCE_IS_WHEN_RECORDS_MOVE_ONE_MASS_PER_RECORD_NO_ACTION_ACROSS_EMPTY_SPACE_SCREENED_DENSITY_POTENTIAL_SIGNED_TILT_CHANNEL_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-20.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORDS_AS_BEABLES_UNDER_THE_MOVING_RECORDS_READING_BELLS_JUMP_LAW_GIVES_NEAREST_NEIGHBOUR_MOVES_EQUIVARIANT_ODDS_AND_BELL_CORRELATIONS_WITH_NONLOCAL_ODDS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L02", "L03", "L04", "L14", "L01-W7"]}
{"id": "L01-W9", "lane": "L01", "title": "One record per site breaks the exact conservation books and leaves the exchange sign open", "plain": "Letting a site hold at most one record turns records into an interacting gas. For free walkers that can share a site, energy and momentum are exactly conserved and the gravity route works. With hard-core exclusion the conservation fails at third order and no local fix restores it. The axioms also do not say whether swapping two identical records gives a plus or a minus.", "severity": "major", "status": "open", "evidence": ["/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/books-program-20260925.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/panel-20260926-after-records-no-go.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_EXACT_BOOKS_NEED_RECORDS_THAT_NEVER_SCATTER_OR_BIND_NOTHING_LOCAL_KEEPS_THEM_UNDER_ONE_RECORD_PER_SITE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-25.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_ONE_RECORD_PER_SITE_KEEPS_THE_BOOKS_ONLY_AT_LEADING_ORDER_TWO_EXCLUDED_RECORDS_LOSE_THEIR_ENERGY_CURRENT_IN_TWO_AND_THREE_DIMENSIONS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-25.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_ONE_RECORD_PER_SITE_NO_POSSIBILITY_SHIFT_AMONG_NEIGHBOURS_RESTORES_THE_BOOKS_NO_NEIGHBOUR_COIN_TERM_KEEPS_TWO_EXCLUDED_RECORDS_ENERGY_CURRENT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-25.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THE_EXCHANGE_SIGN_IS_NOT_SUPPLIED_BY_RECORDS_BOTH_HARD_CORE_SECTORS_MEET_EVERY_AXIOM_AND_FIRST_DIFFER_IN_THE_FOURTH_MOMENT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_UNDER_ONE_RECORD_PER_SITE_A_COLLISION_CHANGES_THE_RECORDS_TWO_STEP_MOMENTUM_ONLY_AT_THIRD_ORDER_IN_THEIR_OFFSETS_FROM_THE_CONES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-26.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORD_READOUT_LOCALITY_READ_AS_LOCAL_TOMOGRAPHY_ADMITS_THE_ORDINARY_COMPOSITE_AND_EXCLUDES_THE_GRADED_ONE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L14", "L05", "L01-W8"]}
{"id": "L01-W10", "lane": "L01", "title": "Which record is which: identity and the beable are chosen, not derived", "plain": "In the moving-records picture a record hops between neighbouring sites, but the law that moves them moves unlabelled occupations. Whether 'the record' travels with a particle depends on a naming rule the dynamics does not fix. Following the record that hops, it stays home while the disturbance runs off. Naming by the wave's own bookkeeping makes it travel, but that changes with how the wave is written.", "severity": "minor", "status": "possibly misframed", "evidence": ["/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/records-are-the-grain.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/records-move-owner-reading.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORDS_AS_BEABLES_UNDER_THE_MOVING_RECORDS_READING_BELLS_JUMP_LAW_GIVES_NEAREST_NEIGHBOUR_MOVES_EQUIVARIANT_ODDS_AND_BELL_CORRELATIONS_WITH_NONLOCAL_ODDS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md", "docs/RECORDS_AS_BEABLES_WHICH_RECORD_CARRIES_A_DISTURBANCE_IS_A_CHOICE_OF_IDENTITY_HOP_FOLLOWING_RECORDS_LAG_A_LAPLACE_IDENTITY_TRAVELS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-28.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L03", "L05", "L01-W7"]}
{"id": "L01-W11", "lane": "L01", "title": "Records give an order of events, not a rate: 'time is the creation of records' has no clock", "plain": "A record history tells you what came before what, and counts records. It does not give a rate. The owner's reading, 'time is the shifting or creation of records', would make local time the local event rate. But events that commute propagate nothing, and a rate needs a physical clock the record order does not supply. A frozen region would be a stopped clock, yet the gravity lane's clocks are assumed to tick.", "severity": "major", "status": "possibly misframed", "evidence": ["/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/panel-20260928b-dilution-and-tolman.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/records-count-rises-until-frozen.md", "docs/A_LAPSE_SET_BY_RECORD_EVENTS_AT_LINEAR_ORDER_POSITIVE_RECORD_KINETICS_EITHER_KEEP_EINSTEINS_NEGATIVE_SCALAR_OR_ADD_A_SCALAR_GRAVITON_THE_CLOSING_LAPSE_NEEDS_THE_DEWITT_LINE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-28.md", "docs/EMERGENT_METRIC_CONFORMAL_CLASS_FROM_RECORDS_SCALE_IS_THE_CLOCK_RATE_NO_GO_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-06.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORD_HISTORY_ORDER_TIME_RATE_FIREWALL_2026-06-05.md", "docs/TIME_AXIS_IS_THE_HISTORY_INDEX_RECORD_MONOTONE_DIRECTION_BOUNDED_NOTE_2026-07-03.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L04", "L14", "L16", "L01-W2"]}
{"id": "L01-W12", "lane": "L01", "title": "Gauss-law (ice-rule) states are not outputs of directed local formation", "plain": "The 'photon from a neighbourhood constraint' route needs states where every vertex obeys a balance rule (the ice rule). Tested as the outcome of records forming one after another from local information, no local order, rule or record scheme produces it. The exceptions add a coordinator site or a non-local plan. A balance rule constrains both sides of a neighbourhood at once, while formation reads only the earlier side.", "severity": "major", "status": "open", "evidence": ["docs/ICE_SUPPORT_UNDER_NEAREST_NEIGHBOUR_FORMATION_VERTEX_BOUND_SOLDERED_VERTEX_RECORDS_ORDER_DEPENDENT_DEFECTS_AND_UNIFORM_ICE_ONLY_BY_CONDITIONING_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/THE_LANDED_TORUS_UNIFORM_ICE_MEASURE_ADMITS_NO_LOCAL_FORMATION_ORDER_EVEN_WITH_EVERY_COORDINATOR_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-23.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md", "docs/UNIFORM_ICE_BY_FORMATION_THE_SQUARE_LOOP_OBSTRUCTION_THE_PLAQUETTE_COORDINATOR_AND_PLANS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md", "docs/UNIFORM_ICE_BY_JOINT_CELL_UNITS_ROWS_YES_THE_TWO_BY_TWO_BLOCK_NO_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-23.md", "docs/UNIFORM_ICE_BY_LAYER_UNITS_ON_INFINITE_PRISMS_IS_EXACT_IN_THE_ZERO_FLUX_SECTOR_THAT_LONG_PRISMS_SELECT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-23.md", "docs/UNIFORM_ICE_BY_SINGLE_SITES_NO_PLANAR_WINDOW_OF_SIX_SQUARES_ADMITS_A_LOCAL_FORMATION_ORDER_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md"], "same_as": ["L06", "L14", "L01-W1"]}
{"id": "L01-W13", "lane": "L01", "title": "Frozen box versus black-hole entropy: no rule and no identified entropy", "plain": "The owner's picture: a box fills with records until it is frozen, and a frozen box is a black hole. Black-hole entropy grows with the area. For the simplest crowding rules the number of possible frozen states grows with the volume instead, and for other rules it is unknown or unique. Which rule, and which quantity counts as entropy, are not fixed.", "severity": "minor", "status": "open", "evidence": ["/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/records-count-rises-until-frozen.md", "docs/SCALE_REFERENCE_PRIMITIVE_NOTE.md", "docs/THE_OWNERS_FROZEN_BOX_READING_WITH_COUNT_THRESHOLD_FORMATION_RULES_UPWARD_RULES_FREEZE_INTO_ONE_STATE_CROWDING_RULES_INTO_MANY_EXACT_SMALL_BOX_COUNTS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-29.md", "docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md"], "same_as": ["L15", "L01-W2", "L01-W11"]}
{"id": "L01-W14", "lane": "L01", "title": "The record statistical bridge and the composition premise are unadopted", "plain": "The axioms give odds for which possibility a forming record locks. They give no odds or frequencies for whether and when records form, and no rule for how records combine. An earlier campaign proposed one postulate (formation odds equal normalized weights of the committed action). The owner parked it. So frequency language stays conditional, and the composition premise C-add is carried as a named premise.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced (equivalent to a named premise)", "evidence": ["docs/ACTION_TRANSFER_RECORD_HAZARD_CONTENT_CROSSCALIBRATION_BOUNDARY_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-02.md", "docs/A_FORMATION_RATE_RULER_EVADES_THE_SEAS_SUBLATTICE_CANCELLATION_AND_THE_BRIDGES_CONSTANT_MODE_FIXES_KAPPA_R_EQUALS_ONE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-04.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md", "docs/RECORD_DURABILITY_DERIVES_GRANULARITY_NOT_WEIGHT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-09.md", "docs/repo/DEFERRED_DECISIONS.md"], "same_as": ["L03", "L02", "L01-W2"]}
{"id": "L01-W15", "lane": "L01", "title": "The motion rule of moving records and the new binding constant", "plain": "In the owner's picture records hop to neighbouring empty sites 'when the neighbourhood allows'. Two readings of 'allows' give different physics. One has the static law as equilibrium and records that clump. The other has an arrow inside the motion and no clumping. The clumping strength is a new dimensionless number that the axioms' normalized odds cannot see.", "severity": "minor", "status": "priced (equivalent to a named premise)", "evidence": ["/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/records-move-owner-reading.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_BINDING_SCALE_PINNED_AT_THE_NEUTRAL_VALUE_PAIR_WEIGHT_IS_THE_RULES_LIKELIHOOD_RATIO_NO_BINDING_WITHOUT_A_CYCLE_ALL_BINDING_IS_AGREEMENT_AROUND_LOOPS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-20.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_RECORDS_THAT_MOVE_PAIR_WEIGHT_TRANSIT_HAS_THE_STATIC_LAW_AS_EQUILIBRIUM_THE_BINDING_SCALE_IS_A_NEW_CONSTANT_CLUMPING_AND_JAMMING_EXECUTED_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-20.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_RECORDS_THAT_MOVE_WITH_VACANCIES_THE_INFRARED_STIFFNESS_IS_SET_BY_THE_BINDING_SCALE_LONG_RANGE_ORDER_ABOVE_THE_NEUTRAL_SCALE_AND_NO_FULL_BOUND_AT_IT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_WHERE_MOVING_RECORDS_CANNOT_CLUMP_A_SHARP_ONE_SITE_BOUND_GIVES_UNIQUENESS_BELOW_A_RATIO_SPREAD_OF_49_OVER_25_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-23.md", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md"], "same_as": ["L02", "L16", "L01-W1"]}
